---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { AUTHOR_NAME, CONTACT_EMAIL, LAST_UPDATED, SITE_NAMES } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
const lang = 'en';
---
<PageLayout title={`Editorial policy – ${SITE_NAMES[lang]}`} description="Where the Italian fines, points and camera register published here come from, who answers for them, how often they are reread, and what happens when an error is reported." lang={lang} noindex={true} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Editorial policy' }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <h1>Editorial and corrections policy</h1>
    <p>A wrong amount makes people pay too much or miss the 5-day discount; a wrong deadline makes an appeal arrive late. Here is where our figures come from and what we do when one of them is wrong.</p>
    <h2>Responsibility</h2><p>{AUTHOR_NAME} answers for every amount, number of points, deadline and calculation in the tools. A figure that does not match its source can be reported to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.</p>
    <h2>Primary sources only</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>the Italian Highway Code and its Regulation</strong>, in the text in force on Normattiva, and the laws amending them;</li>
      <li><strong>the points table of article 126-bis</strong>, read row by row;</li>
      <li><strong>the register of speed-measuring devices</strong> of the Ministry of Infrastructure and Transport (CC BY 3.0 IT);</li>
      <li><strong>the ISTAT list of comuni</strong> (CC BY 4.0), to attach each device to its comune.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>No figure is taken from an appeal service, law firm, insurer or forum. A penalty we could not check against a text in force is not published.</p>
    <h2>The range in the text, never a forecast</h2><p>We give the minimum and maximum the text sets. We do not predict what a prefetto or a judge will decide and promise no outcome for an appeal.</p>
    <h2>Checks before publication</h2><p>The method’s examples, the bounds of every band and the deadlines are tests; an update that fails them is blocked. A register of fewer than 3,000 devices is rejected, and each amount is checked against a literal sentence of the law.</p>
    <h2>Update schedule</h2><p>Legal texts: reread on Normattiva; the date of the latest reread is shown on every page. Speed-camera register: a weekly reread is planned, but no direct read of the ministry site has succeeded so far; the pages use the copy archived by the Internet Archive on 22/02/2026.</p>
    <h2>Handling errors</h2>
    <ol><li>Checked against the text in force.</li><li>Parameters or code corrected, a test added.</li><li>New date on the pages concerned.</li></ol>
    <h2>Independence</h2><p>No commercial link with any lawyer, appeal service, driving school or insurer. No sponsored links in the texts. Any commercial relationship would be stated plainly.</p>
    <p>See also the <a href={route('method', lang)}>method</a>. Version: {LAST_UPDATED}.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
